# CPEye Architecture

## Runtime stack (authoritative)

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Framework | Next.js 16 App Router, React 19 |
| UI | shadcn/ui + Tailwind v4 (`@/components/ui/*`) |
| DB | better-sqlite3 → `data/cpe-monitor.db` |
| Auth | jose JWT in httpOnly cookie `token`, bcryptjs passwords |
| Jobs | node-cron + in-process intervals (`src/lib/scheduler.ts`) |
| CPE | `src/lib/cpe-client.ts` (SRP login, session cache) |

**Not runtime truth** (docs/deps may be stale): Neon Postgres, HeroUI, Vercel serverless, active Drizzle query usage. Prefer `package.json` + `src/lib/*` over README when they conflict.

## Module ownership

| Concern | Own here |
|---------|----------|
| CPE HTTP/protocol | `src/lib/cpe-client.ts` only — do not open parallel CPE clients |
| Collection, alerts, SMS sync, daily report cron | `src/lib/scheduler.ts` |
| SQLite open + `initializeDatabase()` | `src/lib/db.ts` |
| Session / password / JWT | `src/lib/auth.ts` |
| Shared domain types | `src/types/` |
| Email / WeCom notify | `src/lib/notifiers/*` |
| Report aggregation | `src/lib/report-generator.ts` |
| Display formatters | `src/lib/format.ts` |
| HTTP API | `src/app/api/**/route.ts` |
| Authenticated UI | `src/app/(authenticated)/**` |

## Data flow

```
UI → API routes → auth + db + cpe-client
scheduler → cpe-client + db + notifiers
```

- Prefer real-time CPE data; fall back to SQLite history when CPE is unavailable
- Side effects (starting scheduler) must stay explicit and idempotent (`ensureSchedulerStarted`)

## Product conventions

- User-facing API error strings may stay **Chinese** for consistency with existing routes
- Path alias: `@/*` → `./src/*`
- Prefer extending existing modules over new parallel stacks
